    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "There have been a lot of parallels made between the 1980 presidential election when Ronald Reagan defeated Jimmy Carter on a landslide to where we are today in 2024. So will Joe Biden go down and defeat like Jimmy Carter did? And what parallels are there? We're going to talk to a man who was elected to the Senate in 1980 and has been serving ever since. That man is Senator Chuck Grassley of Iowa. He's a legend in the Senate, and I'm so honored to have him on the show. I have so many questions from, but what we are going to talk to him about is how is he so liked? We live in such a politically toxic world where everyone hates each other, but somehow conservatives love him, moderates love him, and even Democrats seem to love the guy. So how does he manage to do that? Well, so talk to him about that 1980 election. Does he think Donald Trump? is gonna have the same victory. And of course we're gonna get his take on his time as chairman of the Senate Judiciary Committee during that Supreme Court nomination of Justice, or now Justice, Brett Kavanaugh. I could tell he was deeply troubled during that process, so we'll talk to him a little bit about that. And lastly, about the weaponization of government. Trust me, you're not gonna wanna miss this interview with a legend of the Senate and just a legend in life, Senator Chuck Grassley of Iowa. Hi, Senator. It's such an honor to have you on the show. You're a legend, so I'm so excited about this.",
