  {
    "episode_id": 94801,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94801.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "When Democrats tried to shut down the Kavanaugh hearing, I think, you know, you don't shut down a hearing. You can shut down, try to shut down an executive meeting of the committee, but not a hearing. So they kept trying to adjourn the hearing. And I decided to put up with it and fight it, but not fight it by gaveling people down, but by letting them talk, and I irritated my Republicans more than I did the Democrats because they thought I ought to shut them up right away. But it takes longer to shut up people that are complaining that it is the let them talk. So I, instead of a meeting, that first meeting getting over and by two o'clock and got over, I guess, by five o'clock. So we wasted three hours, but they didn't run over me.",
