    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Inflation, mostly. Higher interest rates was a big factor. And I think it's related to that, but how it affects the economy. Now, this administration is trying to say, well, interest rates have gone down from nine, a high of nine to three. They forget it was 1.4 when they took office. and what they want people to feel good about, like inflation is gone. Well, increased inflation is gone, but for a family of four in Iowa, I see the figure close to $7,000 a year. In the case of big cities for a family of four, maybe $10,000 a year, that Biden inflation is branded into their their family budget for the rest of their life. It's never going to go away. And that's pretty important. And then you've got this Biden border crisis is unlike anything we've seen before. It's unparalleled in American history. And that's a major issue as well. Now you want me, I guess, I just mentioned immigration. That was not a problem in the Carter administration, but it's surely a problem for this administration.",
