  {
    "episode_id": 94801,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94801.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "Well, I don't know because civil servants or even political appointees, at least on the justice department, FBI should throw politics to the side, but the way that they worked on Trump, even before he was elected, that he was a Russian agent, the way they are using the courts now to do it, they haven't put politics aside. And I sure hope that we have a President Trump that will not, he will forget this word about retribution. I think maybe he has. I haven't heard him talk about it much. But this President Trump has an opportunity to do what Biden said he was going to do in the last election and his inaugural bring people together. They've divided America up into religious secular people. black and white people, Hispanics, separate from blacks and from Asians. And I don't know how many different divisions we have. We're all Americans. And I want Kennedy Trump, hopefully Trump presidency to do what Biden said he was going to do on inaugural day. bring America together, but he's done just exactly the opposite. And I think it has caused Americans to lose faith in our institutions, like the FBI. And I want to give you an example of one person that I whistle blowers helped me bring to the public's attention, Tebow. And it's spelled in a French way. It's a good example where we had whistleblowers say, you need to look at this guy's, what he's doing and what his social media says. And we got proof that he was starting investigations against Trump on lousy newspaper information. He was stopping investigations of Hunter Biden when there was evidence they should proceed. And he was in charge of starting and stopping all these investigations. And I pointed out to Ray, probably the only time Ray ever did anything that I asked him to do, but he fired the guy, or at least the guy is gone. And then another one is this 1023 example, where I heard from whistleblowers and FBI, and they brought to me this 1023. It took me several months to actually get my hands on it, but they told me what was in it. And even before I got my hands on it, I was trying to get information. What are you doing about this information? No answers. And then even after I made it public July of last year, it was September 27th before they started questioning this guy. I think his name's Smirov. And I never knew who he was. Didn't know he existed. I didn't say that what was in the 1023 was truthful or not truthful. I just wanted to know what the FBI was doing. And we found out that this document was existed since June 2020. And here 2023, almost the end of 2023, they started investigating it. Now, if I hadn't made this 1023 public, This guy had been working for the FBI, paid a couple hundred thousand dollars over a period of 10, I suppose now you'd say 13 years, and he would still be lying to the FBI. And he would still be being paid by the taxpayers and still maybe be an agent for the for the Russians. I don't know for that for sure. But those are some of the things that my oversight has done to make sure the FBI does its job. Hopefully if they do their job, they're going to reestablish their credibility. But that's why oversight is so important. The checks and balances of government that you learn in eighth grade civics. And I'm going to keep it up. But I want I want to know whether the FBI is earning their money and and or they doing are they being political and I think they weren't investigating this guy because they didn't want to they didn't want to get in the Hunter Biden situation right and my 1023 forced them to get a person they had been paying for and trusting. In fact, Ray testified to Congress that he was a credible source of information. So even Ray didn't know what was going on,",
